      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: If `sys.executable` contains spaces (which is very common on Windows, e.g., `C:\\Program Files\\Python310\\python.exe`), this new code will cause a regression on Windows.\n\nPreviously, Ninja executed this unquoted command string via `CreateProcessA`, which has a special fallback to magically handle unquoted executable paths with spaces. However, the new code passes the command to `cmd.exe /s /c` (on line 325), which does not have this fallback. `cmd.exe` will split the unquoted executable path at the first space and fail (e.g. `\u0027C:\\Program\u0027 is not recognized as an internal or external command`).\n\nTo fix this, you should quote `sys.executable`. For example:\n```python\n  sys_exec \u003d f\u0027\"{sys.executable}\"\u0027 if host.is_windows() else shlex.quote(sys.executable)\n  cmd \u003d \u0027%s %s%s\u0027 % (sys_exec, rel_self, args)\n```",
